The function is already minimal, so the gain can only be small. The rewrite keeps the same logic and behavior but:
- reads `profile` into a local once;
- marks the explicit-type path as the likely branch, so the compiler lays out the common case as straight-line code.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 t = type;
    if (__builtin_expect(t != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1))
        return t;

    const Profile::MESG* const p = profile;
    if ((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[profileIndex].type;
}
```